• Perform feasibility and impact analysis, architecture design, and development of tools and enhancements using advanced technologies and Oracle PeopleSoft system using 8.57;

• Improve scalability, speed, and performance of existing models;

• Create various documentation required as part of implementation;

• Design and build web services to integrate Oracle PeopleSoft with third party systems in real-time;

• Design, monitor, and enhance data conversion program;

• Produce various documentation required as part of implementation;

• Ability to meet the timelines set by the support centre on the Change requests raised;

• Prepare roll-out plan for the various development activities;

• Develop integration mechanisms between HR and other systems;

• Support migration plan and procedures;

• Prepare POC, feasibility study for new requirements;

• Peer review for new change requests;

Profile:

• Bachelor or Master degree;

• 3+ years of technical development experience in PeopleSoft v9.x (v9.2 preferred) Human Capital Management modules, including LMS, Recruiting/TAM;

